import Mathlib
import ChallengeDeps

/-!
# The frozen statement of o048, cut into named pieces

`PlankEstimate`, `SlopeVolumeEstimate`, `TerminalChartAssertion` and `DK4` are the four parts of
the frozen type, verbatim. `TCAHyp` collects the antecedents of the terminal-chart assertion for
given data and `TCAConcl` is its conclusion at a time exponent `h`; `tca_apply` applies the
assertion. The proof is split at `SlopeDominated`:

* the construction (paper Theorem 2.17, smoothing, homogenization, endpoint selection and crop)
  proves `PlankEstimate → ¬ DK4 → ConstructionOutput`;
* the comparison (paper Theorem 2.17, positive horizon) proves that a slope-dominated problem
  has no true terminal system at small time exponents, using `SlopeVolumeEstimate`.
-/

set_option linter.unusedVariables false

namespace Submission.Obl.k4_discrete_of_terminal_charts

